# leapfrog-energy-step.test on a GPU, in double and in mixed precision:
# under leapfrog a step that writes a row of energies leaves the state of
# the plain step to the bit (#285), and in double precision the positions
# are those of velocity Verlet within 1e-11 nm where it takes the same
# steps. Inputs/leapfrog_energy_step.py.
#
# Three of the 17 cases run here by default; all 17 run on the CPU in
# double precision in every suite (leapfrog-energy-step.test), and on a
# GPU in the suite of a release (leapfrog-energy-step-release-gpu.test,
# lit's -Drelease=1).
#
# The three cases, one for each form of the step with constraints (#285):
#   langevin               Langevin dynamics: the velocities change within
#                          the drift, so every program takes the projected
#                          form, the first half kick of velocity Verlet;
#   nve                    constant energy: the step with the virial keeps
#                          the kick of the plain step and takes the drift
#                          of velocity Verlet on the side, for the virial;
#   v-rescale-anisotropic  the scaling step of the barostat with
#                          "TROTTER_FIRST_ORDER" and the anisotropic
#                          coupling, with against without the virial.
# Before the fix the two runs of each of the three differed (by 2.7e-6,
# 2.3e-14, and 4.8e-6 nm on the CPU in double precision).
#
# REQUIRES: hdf5, cuda
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/leapfrog_energy_step.py mdir %S/Inputs %t/double GPU DOUBLE langevin nve v-rescale-anisotropic | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DOUBLE
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/leapfrog_energy_step.py mdir %S/Inputs %t/mixed GPU MIXED langevin nve v-rescale-anisotropic | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MIXED

# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE nve: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE langevin: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: GPU DOUBLE v-rescale-anisotropic: the states are identical; within {{.*}} nm of velocity Verlet
# DOUBLE: leapfrog GPU DOUBLE: 3 of 3 cases passed

# MIXED: GPU MIXED nve: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED langevin: the states are identical
# MIXED: GPU MIXED v-rescale-anisotropic: the states are identical
# MIXED: leapfrog GPU MIXED: 3 of 3 cases passed
